// THE G-BUFFER'S SURFACE CLASS (PHOTON-2 stage 2d): the prepass writes the normals target
// (R10G10B10A2, OgreChain.cpp) with its two-bit alpha at 1 - upstream's constant. FOLIAGE
// (an alpha-tested cut-out or a two-sided surface: Lumen's bHasBackfaceDiffuse class) writes
// 0 there instead, so the screen-probe gather's pixel history (rq_probe_integrate.comp,
// jah_probe_history.glsl) can hold a foliage pixel to its own looser depth test and never
// blend it with a non-foliage history. The hook runs after the body has written the target.
// Atom's decode carries the class in its own properties: atom_two_sided (PBS's two-sided
// lighting, moved by HlmsAtom) and atom_cutout (the bucket's members are alpha-tested; its
// twin tests nothing, the id pass masked the coverage). DISJOINT from every other definition
// of this hook: the gather's blended-prepass discard (alpha blend), the card capture's (its
// own property), the fog's and the photon view's (not the prepass), the hit decode's (its own
// property). A depth-only prepass writes no normals target.
@property( hlms_prepass && !hlms_alphablend && !hlms_shadowcaster && !hlms_render_depth_only && !jah_card_capture && !atom_hit_mode )
@property( alpha_test || two_sided_lighting || atom_two_sided || atom_cutout )
@piece( custom_ps_posExecution )
	outPs_normals.w = _h( 0.0 );
@end
@end
@end
